# T-1563 acceptance gate: scope-frames threading enables VarRef resolution across scope levels.
# Updated for S-926 new API (builtin-scope-new, builtin-resolve doc frames, builtin-eval doc scope-id).
#
# Two-level scope chain:
#   level 0: base scope with x: 10
#   level 1: extended scope with y: 20 (parent = level 0)
# Evaluates [sum: [builtin-int-add x y]] where x and y are at different scope levels.
# Both VarRefs must resolve correctly via the display chain.
#
# NOTE: May OOM during prelude loading (~3.5 GB). T-1586 tracks resolution.
[call [fn [let]
  [base-scope: [builtin-scope-new 0 [x: 10]]]
  [ext-scope:  [builtin-scope-new base-scope [y: 20]]]
  [src:        [builtin-str-bytes "[sum: [builtin-int-add x y]]"]]
  [parsed:     [builtin-parse src "test.llt"]]
  [desugared:  [builtin-desugar parsed.program]]
  [docs:       [builtin-program-docs desugared]]
  [doc:        [builtin-get 0 docs]]
  [frames:     [scope-to-frames ext-scope]]
  [resolved:   [builtin-resolve doc frames]]
  [result:     [builtin-eval resolved.doc ext-scope]]
  [sum-ok:     [builtin-eq-int result.result.sum 30]]
  sum-ok]]
=== out
Int(1)
